{"article_ids": ["1bc03067c0b488a1"], "canonical_title": "SLICE-Mem: Salience-Gated Lightweight Information Curation for Efficient LLM Agent Memory", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.7, "description": "The paper presents SLICE-Mem, a new memory framework for large language model (LLM) agents. It uses a salience‑guided admission mechanism to decide which user turns to retain and a predicate‑centered information extraction process. A compact classifier identifies valuable turns, reducing the need for repeated full LLM inference for memory admission, extraction, and organization.", "entities": ["term:slice"], "first_seen": "2026-10-27T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_1bc03067c0b488a1", "importance_score": 6.34, "last_updated": "2026-10-27T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["5c6a155408a94369"], "canonical_title": "Multi-Agent Retrieval-Augmented Causality Assessment (MARCA) of Individual Case Safety Reports in Pharmacovigilance", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.7, "description": "Researchers introduced MARCA, a four‑agent framework that augments Naranjo‑based causality assessment of individual case safety reports with scientific literature retrieval and drug‑label analysis. The system’s scores were compared to human expert assessments and to scores generated without retrieval augmentation.", "entities": ["term:marca", "term:ra"], "first_seen": "2026-10-27T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_5c6a155408a94369", "importance_score": 6.29, "last_updated": "2026-10-27T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["23d59e9a5bcc0609"], "canonical_title": "OpenAI announces three big science discoveries and a new way to work with academics", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.7, "description": "OpenAI announced three new scientific findings—one each in mathematics, computer science and physics—and said it will work with external academic experts, called “shepherds,” who will guide the AI‑generated research results. This follows a prior release of hundreds of manuscript‑style outputs claiming solutions to longstanding math problems.", "entities": ["org:openai"], "first_seen": "2026-10-26T23:34:58Z", "id": "evt_23d59e9a5bcc0609", "importance_score": 5.893, "last_updated": "2026-10-26T23:34:58Z", "source_ids": ["the-verge-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["6d54c075dc94cc2f"], "canonical_title": "EviGround-CT: Sentence-to-Volume Grounding for Verifying LLM-Generated Chest CT Reports", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "The paper presents EviGround-CT, a system that verifies positive findings in chest CT reports generated by large language models. It first uses a deterministic extractor to locate sentences describing positive findings, then applies a 3D grounding model that predicts an evidence mask for each sentence, preserving anatomical location, laterality, and descriptive modifiers.", "entities": ["term:ct"], "first_seen": "2026-10-27T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_6d54c075dc94cc2f", "importance_score": 5.84, "last_updated": "2026-10-27T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["c6bba90d60fe3883"], "canonical_title": "How OpenAI turned its coding tools into dots, an always-on personal assistant", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.45, "description": "OpenAI repurposed its existing coding tools into a new product called \"dots,\" described as an always‑on personal assistant for developers. The effort is led by OpenAI executive Alexander Embiricos, who is responsible for the dots initiative.", "entities": ["org:openai"], "first_seen": "2026-10-27T02:00:00Z", "id": "evt_c6bba90d60fe3883", "importance_score": 5.793, "last_updated": "2026-10-27T02:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["techcrunch-ai"]}
